add ability to use an external logger for simulator logging.

I thought that could be a quick and easy way to expose logs from the simulator (at least until we will have a proper events logging in the sdk and print support in the language) so the console will be able to show something to the users

usage (in the console we will use ipc to pass the data to the renderer process):

```
    const simulator = new Simulator({
        simfile: appPath,
        logger: {
            info(msg: string, ...obj) {
                console.info(msg, ...obj);
            },
            warn(msg: string, ...obj) {
                console.warn(msg, ...obj);
            },
            error(msg: string, ...obj) {
                console.error(msg, ...obj);
            }
        }
    });
```

@eladb @skyrpex @Chriscbr please let me know what you think about the idea before i'm adding logs around

